don't bother with "dullness/sharpness" modes for weapons! It's a
distracting feature that doesn't NEED to be in the game. the idea
that a whetstone could be used to restore a weapon and provide
enchantment to the limit of +1 seems okay. it takes time, of course,
to do this, let's say ~25 moves to provide 1 enchantment, so that
restoring a -3 long sword to a +1 long sword would take 100
uninterrupted moves. the process can be interrupted, but it requires
25 uninterrupted moves to provide 1 enchantment, so if you get
interrupted you've got to start over again. the whetstone should be
a stone like loadstones and luckstones but it can be applied like a
tool. cursed ones do damage (limit -7), uncursed work as above,
blessed ones have an upper limit of +5. the lifetime of a whetstone
should be about 250 moves while being used and it should weigh about
10x the weight of a normal stone.
